  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We have to divide a positive number $(22)$ by a negative one $(-11).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n22÷(-11)=-\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $22$ by $11$ without any signs: $22÷11=2.$ Therefore,  we get\n\n$$\n22÷(-11)=-2.\n$$",
